    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34936b53_e7a49c93",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.0/IBluetoothAudioProvider.hal",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1318371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-14T18:26:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks to reply and may I say it will cover some cases for sub-session like openProvider(SESSION_HYBRID) -\u003e startSession(SESSION_HYBRID_SW or SESSION_HYBRID_HW)?\nHow about the codecConfig if we limit that developer must to do something like below?\n    openProvider(sessionType, codecConfig) {\n        Provider.init(sessionType, codecConfig);\n        return Provider;\n    }\n    Provider.startSession(subSessionType);\nHow do you think if it can be a well defined?",
      "parentUuid": "685cc9c9_ae63ebb5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0bbb1feb164c17aa8175a025baf7731a7cf8fcec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90ebcd3c_656b117a",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.0/IBluetoothAudioProvider.hal",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1071489
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-14T18:37:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you want to simplify things a bit, you can explicitly restrict/document that\na provider cannot implement more than one sessionType. Then:\n\n1) openProvider(sessionType)\n2) startSession(codecConfig)\n\nI added a comment elsewhere, that codecConfig as a second argument to openProvider\nis wrong so it should be removed (I don\u0027t remember why I had it there in the first\nversion of the CL). Having multiple providers per sessionType AND per\ncodecConfig will create lots of complexity.",
      "parentUuid": "34936b53_e7a49c93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0bbb1feb164c17aa8175a025baf7731a7cf8fcec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc6f15b9_3fec53c5",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.0/IBluetoothAudioProvider.hal",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-14T20:10:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the main question is whether a Provider can be reused. For a particular session type, a provider may work for some codec, but not others. e.g. If a HW encoder only supports SBC and AAC, then the following sequence will result in a failure:\n\n1) openProvider(SESSION_A2DP_HW);\n2) startSession(SBC) -\u003e works\n3) endSession()\n3) startSession(APTX) -\u003e will fail -\u003e BT stack has to re-open another provider\n\nInstead, I think the call flow should be standardized such that BT stack always go through the following sequence:\n\n1) openProvider(SESSION_A2DP_HW, SBC)\n2) startSession() -\u003e returns nothing\n3) endSession()\n4) openProvider(SESSION_A2DP_SW, APTX)\n5) startSession() -\u003e returns the fast message queue\n5) endSession()\n\nIf startSession() takes no parameter, BT stack developer is forced to always call openProvider(sessionType, codecConfig) before calling startSession(), avoiding codec not supported errors like above.",
      "parentUuid": "90ebcd3c_656b117a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0bbb1feb164c17aa8175a025baf7731a7cf8fcec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64aaa09d_1401baad",
        "filename": "bluetooth/audio/2.0/IBluetoothAudioProvider.hal",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1318371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-14T22:01:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "By my viewpoint, the variable is Audio Vendor\u0027s Hal but BT Stack should be fixed to AOSP. It means BT Stack has consistent behavior and based on this assumption, it should be enough to tell Audio Vendor what we will do.\nBack to Jack\u0027s case, since all checks are done by Stack (step#4), it seems to be well for reuse and Stack needs to reopen when this codec is not supported by current session.\nThat is we (BT Stack) will always select the codec which the provider supported and it can just return UNSUPPORTED_CODEC_CONFIGURATION and the exception is handled by Stack.",
      "parentUuid": "cc6f15b9_3fec53c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "0bbb1feb164c17aa8175a025baf7731a7cf8fcec",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
